The '''1996 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match contested between [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]] of [[France]] and [[SK Rapid Wien|Rapid Wien]] of [[Austria]]. It was the final match of the [[1995–96 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]] and the 36th [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup|Cup Winners' Cup]] final. The final was held at [[King Baudouin Stadium]] in [[Brussels]] on 8 May 1996, hosting its first European club final since the scenes of the [[Heysel Stadium disaster]] eleven years prior. Paris Saint-Germain won the match 1–0, thanks to a free kick from [[Bruno Ngotty]].

